  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5379",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to interact with BHY through a shared pathway involving palmarumycin CP18, which acts as a target for multiple downstream molecules. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N directly targets A704, P2X purinoceptor 1, or Ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 5, all of which are targets of palmarumycin CP18. This indicates that Mollicellin N may exert its effects by modulating the activity of palmarumycin CP18, potentially through competitive or inhibitory mechanisms. The consistent presence of palmarumycin CP18 as a mediator between Mollicellin N and BHY supports a role for this compound in the biological response. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Mollicellin N influences BHY, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
